---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Prose from '../components/Prose.astro';
import { GITHUB } from '../lib/links';
---
<Base title="About" description="VoiceGateway is the open-source profiler for voice agents: cost and latency for every STT, LLM and TTS call, on LiveKit and Pipecat, on your own keys.">
  <Prose
    title="VoiceGateway is what we wished we had."
    lead="A voice agent runs three meters at once. STT bills by audio seconds, the LLM by tokens, TTS by characters, and no provider dashboard shows what one conversation cost across all three. VoiceGateway does, with one line in your agent."
  >
    <h2>What it is</h2>
    <p>
      An open-source (AGPL-3.0) engine and a dashboard you run yourself. It records one telemetry row per request, with cost
      and latency, and rolls them up per call, per agent and per project. <code>voicegw reconcile</code> checks the
      totals against your provider’s invoice.
    </p>

    <h2>What it is not</h2>
    <p>
      It is not in your provider keys or your call audio. Your agents run on your own credentials, and VoiceGateway
      sits beside the agent, not between the agent and the provider. There is no hosted version yet; if enough teams
      want one, we will build it.
    </p>

    <h2>How we build it</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Your keys, always.</strong> Provider keys stay on your servers.</li>
      <li><strong>Telemetry, not audio.</strong> Cost and latency metadata only. Conversations never leave your infrastructure.</li>
      <li><strong>Open source at the core.</strong> The whole engine is open source under AGPL-3.0, and the prices it uses come from an open catalog, <a href="https://prices.mahimai.ca">voice-prices</a>.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>The code, the issues and the changelog are on <a href={GITHUB}>GitHub</a>.</p>
  </Prose>
</Base>
